    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0285" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/3–1942</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Welles</hi>)<anchor n="11" xml:id="d212-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-13">April 13, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You may care to glance at this file.</p>
                <p>Unless you perceive objection, FE<anchor n="11a" xml:id="d212-f2"/> will take up
                    with TA<anchor n="12" xml:id="d212-f3"/> the question of setting up a small
                    committee along the lines indicated in the second paragraph of Mr. Hornbeck’s
                    memorandum of April 9.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">axwell</hi>] M. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">amilton</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d212-f1" n="11" type="source" xml:id="d212-f1-content">
                <p>The original of this memorandum, attached to the memorandum by Mr. Adams dated
                    March 19, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg268">p. 268</ref>,
                    bears the notation “O. K. SW”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d212-f2" n="11a" xml:id="d212-f2-content">
                <p>Division of Far Eastern Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d212-f3" n="12" xml:id="d212-f3-content">
                <p>Division of Commercial Treaties and Agreements.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
